  -m 'Legacy fallback prices only main-agent tokens: tokenUsage does not model subagent_tokens

internal/ingest/checkpoint.go:89 declares tokenUsage with the five billable token fields plus cost, but no subagent_tokens field. The CLI types.TokenUsage (cmd/entire/cli/agent/types/token_usage.go) nests a full SubagentTokens *TokenUsage subtree, and the parent flat counts do not include it.

For current checkpoints this is correct and deliberate: the CLI dispatcher remainder bucket attributes subagent shortfall under the session model, so subagent tokens DO appear as their own model_usage entry (see the CalculateModelUsage doc in cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/transcript.go -- "the dispatcher remainder bucket attributes any subagent shortfall under the session model"). Summing model_usage therefore captures them, and reading the nested subtree as well would double-count.

