Here the estimate prices only the flat parent counts, so subagent tokens are silently excluded. Reported cost wins first via bucketCost, so this only bites legacy checkpoints written before the CLI persisted a cost AND before model_usage existed -- a genuinely small set, which is why this is low.

Suggested fix: no behaviour change needed; state the scope in the bucketCost / else-branch doc comment so the omission reads as deliberate rather than as an oversight, and so a future re-price job does not assume the flat totals are complete. If completeness matters, add subagent_tokens to tokenUsage and fold it in on the else-branch only.' 2>&1 | grep -E '"severity"' | head -2

